cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Divisible-Sandpile-RWRS: a Lean 4 formalization of Divisible sandpiles via random walks in random scenery"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of the paper "Divisible
  sandpiles via random walks in random scenery" (Bou-Rabee, Peres and
  Sava-Huss): explosion and stabilization for random walk in random scenery
  (Theorem 1.1), explosion of the divisible sandpile with i.i.d. initial masses
  on infinite bounded-degree graphs for mean above one and at mean one
  (Theorem 1.2), its stabilization below mean one under a moment condition
  (Theorem 1.3), and every other labelled statement of the paper, including
  the sharpness constructions.  Of the nine results the paper cites without
  proof, eight are proved here and one, the ergodic decomposition of stationary
  random networks, is an explicit hypothesis of the statements that use it.
  The development contains no sorry and no custom axiom.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - divisible sandpile
  - random walk in random scenery
  - optimal stopping
  - probability
license: Apache-2.0
